From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] A scripted walk out of the wider picture not stopped by the player's follower (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A walk that ends near the DS's screen edge is made longer on the wider
screen, so the walker goes out of sight before it's taken away. The
check for someone in the way counted the player's follower Pokémon (or
its Poké Ball), which the DS doesn't have. In Mt. Coronet, as Cyrus
left, the follower stood behind the player, so his walk was left as the
DS has it and he vanished in the middle of the wider screen. The
follower and its ball are no longer counted: he now walks on toward
the cave's exit and out of sight.

---
diff --git a/src/scrcmd.c b/src/scrcmd.c
index f23c8588..eee8584d 100644
--- a/src/scrcmd.c
+++ b/src/scrcmd.c
@@ -2408,8 +2408,14 @@ static void ScrCmd_PortWideNoteWalkers(ScriptContext *ctx, MapObject *mapObj, in
     }
 }
 
+#include "port_follower.h"
+
 // Someone standing on (x, z), not walking a script's way (they walk out
-// together), nor the walker or the player.
+// together), nor the walker or the player, nor the player's follower (no
+// one the DS has: it goes with the player. Standing behind the player in
+// Mt. Coronet as Cyrus left, the one step west of him the DS's picture
+// shows, his walk out was taken as blocked there and left as the DS has
+// it: he went 3 tiles inside the wider picture's edge, 2026-11-03).
 static BOOL ScrCmd_PortWideSomeoneThere(FieldSystem *fieldSystem, MapObject *walker, int x, int z)
 {
     MapObject *other;
@@ -2418,7 +2424,7 @@ static BOOL ScrCmd_PortWideSomeoneThere(FieldSystem *fieldSystem, MapObject *wal
 
     while (MapObjectMan_FindObjectWithStatus(fieldSystem->mapObjMan, &other, &i, MAP_OBJ_STATUS_0) == TRUE) {
         if (other == walker || other == player || MapObject_CheckStatus(other, MAP_OBJ_STATUS_4)
-            || ScrCmd_PortWideIsWalker(other)) {
+            || ScrCmd_PortWideIsWalker(other) || MapObject_PortIsFollower(other)) {
             continue;
         }
 
